{"author":{"id":"686d9350e5e426946f54ca7a73ceeef9fd8682b44ea6617ce58187e451c43768"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790971342,"nonce":"nu8fvX4+vs+DUTal7SQX88FWCDk=","message":"Exercised on 2026-10-02 in headless Chrome on macOS, through Ash's page (Ash d19312b41993d0b2bf909d76f28d40783c4cf869, local, which loads side modules in a page and defines ash_host_watch). One wasm32-wasip1-threads program loaded xgpu.wasm and xwindow.wasm. It opened the canvas as an xwindow window, then created the instance, surface, adapter (via plain `await`), device, buffer, shader and pipeline. It drew a triangle on each RedrawRequested, 361 frames in 6 s, and a screenshot shows it.\n\nIt needed three web-backend gaps filled in xgpu's working tree: compatibleSurface, surface capabilities and adapter info. The other 144 missing natives are xgpu 106cf53fe7b624d802a6e53bffdb0a23e9ef7da8d3e4163cb6a461cb047b05ac. A browser program using textures, samplers, viewports or error scopes still raises.\n\nTo reproduce: scripts/build_wasm.sh and scripts/build_window_wasm.sh into one directory. Then `ASH_WASM_FIBERS=1 ash --build \u003cdir\u003e/program.wasm --target wasm32-wasip1-threads program.hl` and `ash serve \u003cdir\u003e`, and open it in Chrome.","files":null}]}